# Signing material and service account files. EAS keeps credentials on its own
# servers by default, so none of this normally exists here - but it does the
# moment you choose local credentials, and an Android keystore in a public
# repository is the one mistake that cannot be walked back: whoever holds it
# can sign updates to your app.
*.keystore
*.pem
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
credentials.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
*.orig.*
